MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_001: I just can't get over it. The moment she saw me...\nDamn, that stung.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_002: Hey, Tobes! What's going on? You look a little down.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_003: My face has never scared you off, has it?
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_004: 'Cause just now I ran into this little girl who started\ncrying as soon as she saw me.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_005: I know I ain't a guy you wanna run into in an alley,\nbut I was just handing her something she dropped.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_006: Seriously? What a brat. You're a cutie, Tobes.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_007: A cutie? Baw haw haw! You don't gotta go\nthat far over the top to cheer me up.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_008: No, I meant it! It's what I really think. Why else\nwould I call you "Tobes"?
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_009: Look into my eyes. Just look. Does it look like I'm\nlying here?
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_010: Wow. You look serious as the grave. Not sure I can\ntake your word for it though.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_011: Oh, come on. You're cheerful, your smile is charming\nas all get-out, and then there's your personality.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_012: Compared to my dad, you're the polar opposite\nof scary.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_013: Well, that's all nice to hear, but— Really? Your dad's\nthat mean looking?
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_014: Oh yeah! And he was beloved. He single-handedly\nunited eight hundred ruffians into one crew.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_015: Eight hundred's nothing to sneeze at. It's like he was\na pilus prior. Not bad!
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_016: Those guys adored Dad. And the ones I met all had\nfaces like yours, Tobes. They were like uncles to me.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_017: "These guys are my brothers," he'd say. "Ah, they're\nas tough as a basket of kittens, deep down."
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_018: So, yeah. I think you're pretty cute, Tobes. As cute\nas any of my uncles.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_019: Alright. Though it sounds like your dad's influence\ngave you some rose-colored glasses.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_020: Hehe. A great man who somehow convinced you\nto see me as cute? I'd love to meet him.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_021: You can't. He's dead.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_022: Oh, uh...sorry if I put my foot in my mouth.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_023: Don't worry about it. It was a long time ago.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_024: Got it. Hey, why don't you let me buy you a drink\nto apologize?
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_025: Are you sure you want to do that? I'm not exactly\na lightweight.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_026: Baw haw haw! Pigs'll fly the day I see a lady\noutdrink me. Do your worst.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_027: Then OK! But the tavern around here is no good.\nLet's go somewhere else.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_028: Whaddaya mean no good? There's nothin' wrong\nwith the drinks here.
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_029: Well, a while back I drank it dry, so they barred me...\nfor life. Ehehe...
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_030: Actually, I wonder if there are any taverns nearby\nwhere they'll still let me in...
MID_SE_Tob_Sop_C_031: Feeling the sudden urge to check the sky for pigs...